* the game isnt about grades of timing or power, its about informational mechanical outplay. you cant come to the fight early or late, your always there at teh right time. its never foiling the enemy, its always full victory, the logic toggles say win/lose



* players need to know about a threat to make them take action
    - the information they have logically means that if they dont take action, a evil guy will make innocent people suffer
    - they are give certain info
        ~ what/how, it needs to be clear to the player, 'if this, then very bad'
        ~ when, still time before it happens, chance to stop it
        ~ mechanics that would cause it to fail
    - they will see from the plan builder that if they dont stop it, then many people will die and therefore there will be a big points spike and the game will end and they will do badly
    - their goal is to win at the game so they should be motivated to do what they can to stop the bad thing
